        <span class="sectionTag">Our story</span>
        <h2>About Us:</h2>
        <div class="postParagraph">
            <span class="postBlock">Hello! We are Kassie and Nicola from New Zealand.</span>
            <span class="postBlock">In 2025 we decided we were too young for boring office jobs, and quit our jobs and packed up our lives to travel the world. We're currently based in Madrid, Spain working part-time as English language assistants in schools. This leaves us plenty of time to explore Europe!</span>
            <span class="postBlock">We are doing so very much on a budget (you're more likely to find us stuffing our faces with local street food than at an expensive attraction). Our ethos is simple; we rate places on budget, food, and how safe we felt as a queer couple in each place.</span>
            <span class="postBlock">We hope to empower other queer travellers to explore this beautiful world in a way that is both safe and wallet-friendly.</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="editorialNotes">
    <div>
        <span class="sectionTag">Budget</span>
        <h3>We love a hostel and a weird route.</h3>
        <p>Some of our favourite trips have been the ones that were exactly in the off-season, when a hostel is half the price and the streets are less crowded.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
        <span class="sectionTag">Safety</span>
        <h3>We're a queer couple - safety is important.</h3>
        <p>We want to see the whole world - sometimes that means going places that aren't so queer-friendly. We take extra precautions and always do our research!</p>
    </div>
    <div>
        <span class="sectionTag">Slow</span>
        <h3>We're anti-checklist travel.</h3>
        <p>What's the point in seeing something just to see it? We care about good experiences, even if that takes longer than normal.</p>
    </div>
</section>
